---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ContactInfo from '../../../components/ContactInfo.astro';
---

<Layout lang="en" title="Biography — Ilian Simeonow"  description="Biography of Ilian Simeonow: graduate of the State Ballet School Berlin, trampoline stunt performer and international stuntman." heroImage="/images/portrait/Portr%C3%A4tfoto-9.jpg">

  <div class="page-hero page-hero--standard">
    <div class="hero-top-bar"></div>
    <div class="page-hero-content">
      <div class="section-label">// Biography</div>
      <h1 class="page-hero-title">Ilian<br /><span style="color: var(--orange);">Simeonow</span></h1>
      <p class="page-hero-sub">Stuntman · Stunt Performer · Artist · Actor</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="bio-section">
    <div class="bio-grid">
      <div class="bio-text">
        <div class="section-label">// About</div>
        <h2 class="section-heading">The Road<br />to Stuntman.</h2>
        <p class="body-text">
          Ilian Simeonow was born on 13 February 1980 in Dresden. His mother, Irina Simeonow (née Schönball), was an active athlete from 1964 to 1977 — DDR youth champion and DDR national champion in sports acrobatics — and has been a coach at PSV Dresden since 1989 (sports acrobatics and trampoline). His father, Stefan Iliev Simeonow, worked as a truck driver for a coal merchant and, after reunification, for a furniture moving company; he is now retired.
        </p>
        <p class="body-text" style="margin-top: 18px;">
          His brother Marko attended KJS Dresden (Children's and Youth Sports School, diving) and, in 1989 during a time of upheaval, enrolled at the <strong style="color: var(--white);">State Ballet School and School for Performing Arts Berlin</strong>. He specialised in teeterboard acrobatics; his other disciplines include the Wheel of Death, trampoline and Globe of Speed — with the latter, he entered the Guinness Book of Records in 1999.
        </p>
        <p class="body-text" style="margin-top: 18px;">
          Ilian spent his first six school years at the 35th Secondary School in Dresden, followed by four more years at the 36th Secondary School. He then completed a 5½-year training as a diploma artist at the State Ballet School Berlin, where he also learned to play guitar and discovered the secrets of magic. From the age of eight, his dream was to become a stuntman.
        </p>
        <p class="body-text" style="margin-top: 18px;">
          After his engagement in 2000/2001 at the Friedrichstadtpalast Berlin, he was called up on 2 January 2002 and completed his military service with the 2nd Parachute Battalion 373 in Doberlug-Kirchhain. In 2004 he joined the stunt team "Artist of Stunt", followed by two years of intensive training and numerous stunt shows. In 2006 he founded his own stunt team, <em style="color: var(--white);">Action Artist</em>, with a unique concept: half the team consisted of acrobats and extreme performers, opening up a new niche. Due to stress culminating in a heart attack, the team was disbanded in 2009 — though the deep friendships and collaborations continue to this day.
        </p>
        <p class="body-text" style="margin-top: 18px;">
          Since 2005, Ilian has been a regular rider with the Globe of Speed team, and since 2008 a Wheel of Death runner. In 2003 he worked for a full year as a teeterboard acrobat and high diver, and has been performing as a magician since 2000. His ability to quickly absorb, recall and execute movement sequences has allowed him to establish himself across many genres — many consider him one of the most versatile all-rounders, artists and stuntmen in the business.
        </p>
        <p class="body-text" style="margin-top: 18px;">
          Ilian is based in Heiligenhaus and is available for international bookings in film, TV and live productions.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="photo-block" style="margin-bottom: 24px; max-width: 50%; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">
          <img src="/images/portrait/Porträtfoto-1.jpg" alt="Ilian Simeonow" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:3/4;object-fit:cover;display:block;" />
          <div class="photo-caption">Ilian Simeonow · Stuntman</div>
        </div>
        <div class="photo-block" style="max-width: 50%; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">
          <img src="/images/bilder-aside/bruederstreit.png" alt="Ilian and his brother Marko" style="width:100%;display:block;" />
          <div class="photo-caption">Ilian &amp; Brother Marko</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stats-section">
    <div class="section-label">// Physical Data</div>
    <h2 class="section-heading">Physical<br />Specifications.</h2>
    <div class="stats-grid">
      <div class="stat-block"><div class="stat-num">1.75 m</div><div class="stat-label">Height</div></div>
      <div class="stat-block"><div class="stat-num">75 kg</div><div class="stat-label">Weight</div></div>
      <div class="stat-block"><div class="stat-num">Athletic</div><div class="stat-label">Figure</div></div>
      <div class="stat-block"><div class="stat-num">57 cm</div><div class="stat-label">Hat Size</div></div>
      <div class="stat-block"><div class="stat-num">48</div><div class="stat-label">Suit Size</div></div>
      <div class="stat-block"><div class="stat-num">42/43</div><div class="stat-label">Shoe Size</div></div>
      <div class="stat-block"><div class="stat-num">31–33</div><div class="stat-label">Trouser Size</div></div>
      <div class="stat-block"><div class="stat-num">M/L</div><div class="stat-label">Shirt Size</div></div>
      <div class="stat-block"><div class="stat-num">Green</div><div class="stat-label">Eye Colour</div></div>
      <div class="stat-block"><div class="stat-num">97/85/100</div><div class="stat-label">B/W/H</div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sports-section">
    <div class="section-label">// Sports Activities</div>
    <h2 class="section-heading">Sport &amp;<br />Martial Arts.</h2>
    <ul class="sports-list">
      <li><span class="sports-year">1986</span>Diving</li>
      <li><span class="sports-year">1986</span>Football (Dynamo Dresden / Löbtauer Kickers)</li>
      <li><span class="sports-year">1987–1988</span>Table Tennis</li>
      <li><span class="sports-year">1988–1996</span>Sports Acrobatics (PSV Dresden)</li>
      <li><span class="sports-year">1988–1996</span>Trampolining (PSV Dresden – competitive)</li>
      <li><span class="sports-year">1991–1994</span>Taekwondo (Green Belt – PSV Mickten)</li>
      <li><span class="sports-year">1992</span>Judo</li>
      <li><span class="sports-year">1992–1994</span>Handball</li>
      <li><span class="sports-year">2000–2001</span>Thai and Kickboxing</li>
      <li><span class="sports-year">2008–2009</span>Modern Arnis</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="timeline-section">
    <div class="section-label">// Career</div>
    <h2 class="section-heading">Training &amp;<br />Career.</h2>
    <div class="timeline">
      <div class="timeline-item"><div class="timeline-year">1989–1994</div><div class="timeline-content"><div class="timeline-title">State Ballet School Berlin</div><div class="timeline-desc">5½-year training as a certified artist, specialising in trampoline. One of Europe's most prestigious performing arts training institutions.</div></div></div>
      <div class="timeline-item"><div class="timeline-year">1994–2000</div><div class="timeline-content"><div class="timeline-title">International Performing Career</div><div class="timeline-desc">Trampoline stunt performer and artist in international circus and show productions. Performances in Norway, Dubai and other countries.</div></div></div>
      <div class="timeline-item"><div class="timeline-year">2001–2008</div><div class="timeline-content"><div class="timeline-title">Transition to Film Stunts</div><div class="timeline-desc">Expansion into film stunts, fight choreography and horse riding. Building networks in German and international film production.</div></div></div>
      <div class="timeline-item"><div class="timeline-year">2009–2011</div><div class="timeline-content"><div class="timeline-title">Piraten Open Air Theatre</div><div class="timeline-desc">Multi-year collaboration as stuntman and actor in open-air productions.</div></div></div>
      <div class="timeline-item"><div class="timeline-year">2011</div><div class="timeline-content"><div class="timeline-title">The Three Musketeers (Hollywood)</div><div class="timeline-desc">Participation in the international film production as fencer and stuntman.</div></div></div>
      <div class="timeline-item"><div class="timeline-year">2013</div><div class="timeline-content"><div class="timeline-title">La belle &amp; la bête (France)</div><div class="timeline-desc">Stunt double for lead actor Nicolas Gob in the French cinema version of the classic fairy tale.</div></div></div>
      <div class="timeline-item"><div class="timeline-year">2015–2019</div><div class="timeline-content"><div class="timeline-title">Semperoper Dresden &amp; Eldorado Templin</div><div class="timeline-desc">Stuntman for opera productions at the Semperoper and multi-year membership in the ELDORADO Stunt Team Templin.</div></div></div>
      <div class="timeline-item"><div class="timeline-year">2022–2024</div><div class="timeline-content"><div class="timeline-title">Karl-May Festival &amp; Semperoper</div><div class="timeline-desc">Continued collaboration with leading German stages. Stuntman and actor at the Karl-May Festival Radebeul and Felsenbühne Rathen.</div></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="contact-section">
    <div>
      <div class="section-label">// Booking &amp; Contact</div>
      <div class="contact-heading">Book<br />Ilian.</div>
      <p class="contact-sub">Stunt Coordinator · Fight Choreographer<br />Action Performer · Artist · Magician</p>
      <div class="contact-actions">
        <a href="/en/contact/" class="btn-primary">Send Enquiry</a>
        <a href="/pdfs/setcard-en.pdf" download class="btn-ghost">↓ Sedcard PDF</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ContactInfo lang="en" showAddress />
  </section>

</Layout>

<style>
.bio-section { padding: var(--section-pad) var(--page-pad); background: var(--black); border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
.bio-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 80px; align-items: start; }
.stats-section { padding: var(--section-pad) var(--page-pad); background: var(--dark); border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
.stats-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr); gap: 1px; background: var(--border); margin-top: 40px; }
.sports-section { padding: var(--section-pad) var(--page-pad); background: var(--black); border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
.sports-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 40px 0 0; max-width: 640px; }
.sports-list li { display: flex; gap: 32px; padding: 14px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: 14px; color: var(--gray); }
.sports-year { color: var(--orange); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 1px; min-width: 100px; flex-shrink: 0; }
.stat-block { background: var(--dark); padding: 32px 20px; text-align: center; }
.timeline-section { padding: var(--section-pad) var(--page-pad); background: var(--black); border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
.timeline { margin-top: 40px; }
.timeline-item { display: flex; gap: 40px; padding: 24px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
.timeline-year { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 2px; color: var(--orange); font-weight: 600; min-width: 100px; flex-shrink: 0; padding-top: 4px; }
.timeline-title { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 18px; color: var(--white); margin-bottom: 8px; }
.timeline-desc { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: 14px; color: var(--gray); line-height: 1.6; }
</style>
